atlas institutional-delegation-model

architecture institutional-delegation-model
  canonical_name InstitutionalDelegationModel
  owns DelegationEnvelope
  consumes Authority
  consumes InformationPolicy
  consumes CapabilityClosure
  consumes EvidenceClosure
  publishes DelegationEnvelope
  publishes BoundClosure
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Delegation
  layer institutional
  semantic_question What exactly does this estate receive from the estate above it, and what does it remain unable to do?
  purpose Make delegation a bounded, inspectable envelope rather than an inheritance, so a managed client receives a provider closure, an information closure, an effect authority and an evidence release without receiving its operator's whole world.
  maturity architectural
  node_types DelegationEnvelope
  node_types ProviderClosure
  node_types InformationClosure
  node_types EffectAuthority
  node_types EvidenceRelease
  edge_types delegates_to
  edge_types bounds
  invariant delegation is bounded downward; a child estate never receives more than its parent holds
  invariant delegation is not inheritance; an unlisted capability is absent rather than implied
  invariant each envelope declares its provider closure, information closure, effect authority, evidence release and model or provider allowances explicitly
  invariant effect authority is separate from read authority; being able to see a subject never implies being able to change it
  invariant an evidence release names what the child may see of the parent's proof, and defaults to nothing
  invariant revoking an envelope revokes every closure derived from it without requiring the child to cooperate
  forbidden_inference a parent holding a capability -> a child holding it
  forbidden_inference a child reading a subject -> a child being able to effect it
  forbidden_inference a delegation existing -> data flowing across it
  forbidden_inference a credential reaching a resource -> the envelope authorizing that reach
  interacts institutional-root
  interacts institutional-relationship-types
  interacts authority
  source_lineage Generation-10 product topology separation, 2026-08-26
